==Maltese==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|mt|ar|[[إِي]] [[وَ]]|tr=ʔī wa-||yes, by...}}, which is to be followed by someone or something to swear by. Common combinations are, for example, {{m|ar|إِي وَٱللّٰه|tr=ʔī wa-llāh||yes, by God}} or {{m|ar|إِي وَرَبِّي|tr=ʔī wa-rabbī||yes, by my Lord}}. Eventually the following word was left out. Compare the same in {{cog|acw|إِيوَه|tr=ʔīwa}} and similar forms in other dialects. The shift from ''w'' to ''v'' is irregular, and ''iva'' is perhaps the only inherited Maltese word with this phoneme. Although when conversing informally, {{m|mt|ijwa}} (''[[ايوه]]) pronunciation is commonly used amongst others such as {{m|mt|ijja}} and {{m|mt|eħe}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|mt|/ˈiː.va/}}

